INSERT INTO `gpt_generated_recipe` VALUES (1,'pasty','- 2 cups all-purpose flour\n- 1/2 cup butter\n- 1/2 cup water\n- 1 tsp salt\n- 1/2 tsp ground cumin\n- 1/2 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp turmeric powder\n- 1/2 cup boiled potatoes, mashed\n- 1/4 cup peas\n- 1/4 cup carrots, chopped\n- 1/4 cup onions, chopped\n- 1/4 cup cilantro, chopped','1. In a bowl, mix together the flour, salt, and butter until it resembles breadcrumbs. Slowly add water and knead until a smooth dough is formed. Let it rest for 30 minutes.\n2. In a pan, heat some oil and sauté the onions until translucent. Add in the peas, carrots, and spices. Cook until the vegetables are soft.\n3. Add in the mashed potatoes and cilantro. Mix well and cook for another 5 minutes. Remove from heat and let it cool.\n4. Preheat the oven to 375°F (190°C). \n5. Divide the dough into equal-sized balls. Roll out each ball into a circle.\n6. Place a spoonful of the vegetable filling on one half of the circle. Fold over the other half to cover the filling and crimp the edges to seal.\n7. Place the pasties on a baking sheet and bake for 20-25 minutes or until golden brown.\n8. Serve hot with mint chutney or ketchup. Enjoy your Pakistani-style pasties!','Ingredients:\n- 2 cups all-purpose flour\n- 1/2 cup butter\n- 1/2 cup water\n- 1 tsp salt\n- 1/2 tsp ground cumin\n- 1/2 tsp chili powder\n- 1/2 tsp turmeric powder\n- 1/2 cup boiled potatoes, mashed\n- 1/4 cup peas\n- 1/4 cup carrots, chopped\n- 1/4 cup onions, chopped\n- 1/4 cup cilantro, chopped\n\nInstructions:\n1. In a bowl, mix together the flour, salt, and butter until it resembles breadcrumbs. Slowly add water and knead until a smooth dough is formed. Let it rest for 30 minutes.\n2. In a pan, heat some oil and sauté the onions until translucent. Add in the peas, carrots, and spices. Cook until the vegetables are soft.\n3. Add in the mashed potatoes and cilantro. Mix well and cook for another 5 minutes. Remove from heat and let it cool.\n4. Preheat the oven to 375°F (190°C). \n5. Divide the dough into equal-sized balls. Roll out each ball into a circle.\n6. Place a spoonful of the vegetable filling on one half of the circle. Fold over the other half to cover the filling and crimp the edges to seal.\n7. Place the pasties on a baking sheet and bake for 20-25 minutes or until golden brown.\n8. Serve hot with mint chutney or ketchup. Enjoy your Pakistani-style pasties!','Not specified',NULL),(2,'Chapli kebab','- 1 pound ground beef\n- 1 onion, finely chopped\n- 2 green chilies, finely chopped\n- 1 tomato, finely chopped\n- 1/4 cup fresh coriander, chopped\n- 1 teaspoon cumin powder\n- 1 teaspoon coriander powder\n- 1 teaspoon red chili powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon garam masala\n- Salt, to taste\n- 1 egg\n- 1/4 cup besan (chickpea flour)\n- Vegetable oil, for frying','1. In a large mixing bowl, combine the ground beef, onion, green chilies, tomato, coriander, cumin powder, coriander powder, red chili powder, turmeric powder, garam masala, and salt. Mix well to combine all the ingredients.\n2. Add the egg and besan to the mixture to help bind everything together. Mix until everything is well incorporated.\n3. Heat the vegetable oil in a frying pan over medium-high heat.\n4. Take a small portion of the kebab mixture and shape it into a flat patty.\n5. Carefully place the kebab in the hot oil and fry until golden brown on both sides, about 3-4 minutes per side.\n6. Repeat the shaping and frying process with the remaining kebab mixture.\n7. Once all the kebabs are cooked, serve hot with naan or roti, along with mint chutney and sliced onions on the side. Enjoy your delicious and authentic Pakistani-style Chapli kebabs!','Ingredients:\n- 1 pound ground beef\n- 1 onion, finely chopped\n- 2 green chilies, finely chopped\n- 1 tomato, finely chopped\n- 1/4 cup fresh coriander, chopped\n- 1 teaspoon cumin powder\n- 1 teaspoon coriander powder\n- 1 teaspoon red chili powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon garam masala\n- Salt, to taste\n- 1 egg\n- 1/4 cup besan (chickpea flour)\n- Vegetable oil, for frying\n\nInstructions:\n1. In a large mixing bowl, combine the ground beef, onion, green chilies, tomato, coriander, cumin powder, coriander powder, red chili powder, turmeric powder, garam masala, and salt. Mix well to combine all the ingredients.\n2. Add the egg and besan to the mixture to help bind everything together. Mix until everything is well incorporated.\n3. Heat the vegetable oil in a frying pan over medium-high heat.\n4. Take a small portion of the kebab mixture and shape it into a flat patty.\n5. Carefully place the kebab in the hot oil and fry until golden brown on both sides, about 3-4 minutes per side.\n6. Repeat the shaping and frying process with the remaining kebab mixture.\n7. Once all the kebabs are cooked, serve hot with naan or roti, along with mint chutney and sliced onions on the side. Enjoy your delicious and authentic Pakistani-style Chapli kebabs!','Not specified',NULL),(3,'Gulab jamun','- 1 cup milk powder\n- 1/4 cup all-purpose flour\n- 1/4 tsp baking soda\n- 2 tbsp ghee (clarified butter)\n- 1/2 cup milk\n- Oil for deep frying\n\nFor the sugar syrup:\n- 1 cup sugar\n- 1 cup water\n- 1/4 tsp cardamom powder\n- Saffron strands (optional)','1. In a bowl, combine the milk powder, all-purpose flour, and baking soda. Mix well.\n2. Add ghee and milk to the dry ingredients and knead into a soft dough.\n3. Divide the dough into small equal-sized balls and roll them between your palms to form smooth balls.\n4. Heat oil in a deep frying pan over medium heat. Once the oil is hot, reduce the heat to low.\n5. Carefully add the dough balls into the hot oil and fry them on low heat until they turn golden brown.\n6. Meanwhile, in a separate saucepan, combine sugar and water to make the syrup. Stir until the sugar dissolves.\n7. Add cardamom powder and saffron strands to the syrup and let it simmer for a few minutes.\n8. Once the Gulab Jamuns are fried to a golden brown color, remove them from the oil and place them in the sugar syrup. Let them soak for at least 30 minutes before serving.\n\nCalories: Approximately 400 kcal per serving (4 pieces)','Ingredients:\n- 1 cup milk powder\n- 1/4 cup all-purpose flour\n- 1/4 tsp baking soda\n- 2 tbsp ghee (clarified butter)\n- 1/2 cup milk\n- Oil for deep frying\n\nFor the sugar syrup:\n- 1 cup sugar\n- 1 cup water\n- 1/4 tsp cardamom powder\n- Saffron strands (optional)\n\nInstructions:\n1. In a bowl, combine the milk powder, all-purpose flour, and baking soda. Mix well.\n2. Add ghee and milk to the dry ingredients and knead into a soft dough.\n3. Divide the dough into small equal-sized balls and roll them between your palms to form smooth balls.\n4. Heat oil in a deep frying pan over medium heat. Once the oil is hot, reduce the heat to low.\n5. Carefully add the dough balls into the hot oil and fry them on low heat until they turn golden brown.\n6. Meanwhile, in a separate saucepan, combine sugar and water to make the syrup. Stir until the sugar dissolves.\n7. Add cardamom powder and saffron strands to the syrup and let it simmer for a few minutes.\n8. Once the Gulab Jamuns are fried to a golden brown color, remove them from the oil and place them in the sugar syrup. Let them soak for at least 30 minutes before serving.\n\nCalories: Approximately 400 kcal per serving (4 pieces)','Not specified',NULL),(4,'kofta','- 500g minced beef or lamb\n- 1 onion, finely chopped\n- 2 cloves of garlic, minced\n- 1 teaspoon ginger paste\n- 1 teaspoon cumin powder\n- 1 teaspoon coriander powder\n- 1 teaspoon red chili powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder\n- Salt to taste\n- 1/4 cup fresh coriander leaves, chopped\n- 1/4 cup fresh mint leaves, chopped\n- 2 tablespoons gram flour (besan)','1. In a large bowl, combine the minced meat, onion, garlic, ginger paste, cumin powder, coriander powder, red chili powder, turmeric powder, salt, coriander leaves, mint leaves, and gram flour. Mix well until all the ingredients are evenly distributed.\n2. Shape the mixture into small, round balls and place them on a baking tray lined with parchment paper.\n3. Preheat the oven to 180°C (350°F) and bake the koftas for 20-25 minutes, or until they are cooked through and golden brown.\n4. Serve hot with naan bread, rice, or salad.\n\nCalories: Approximately 420 kcal','Ingredients:\n- 500g minced beef or lamb\n- 1 onion, finely chopped\n- 2 cloves of garlic, minced\n- 1 teaspoon ginger paste\n- 1 teaspoon cumin powder\n- 1 teaspoon coriander powder\n- 1 teaspoon red chili powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder\n- Salt to taste\n- 1/4 cup fresh coriander leaves, chopped\n- 1/4 cup fresh mint leaves, chopped\n- 2 tablespoons gram flour (besan)\n\nInstructions:\n1. In a large bowl, combine the minced meat, onion, garlic, ginger paste, cumin powder, coriander powder, red chili powder, turmeric powder, salt, coriander leaves, mint leaves, and gram flour. Mix well until all the ingredients are evenly distributed.\n2. Shape the mixture into small, round balls and place them on a baking tray lined with parchment paper.\n3. Preheat the oven to 180°C (350°F) and bake the koftas for 20-25 minutes, or until they are cooked through and golden brown.\n4. Serve hot with naan bread, rice, or salad.\n\nCalories: Approximately 420 kcal','420 kcal',NULL),(5,'Chicken tikka','- 500g boneless chicken, cut into cubes\n- 1 cup yogurt\n- 2 tbsp ginger-garlic paste\n- 1 tbsp red chili powder\n- 1 tsp turmeric powder\n- 1 tsp garam masala\n- 1 tbsp lemon juice\n- Salt to taste\n- 2 tbsp oil','1. In a bowl, mix yogurt, ginger-garlic paste, red chili powder, turmeric powder, garam masala, lemon juice, and salt.\n2. Add the chicken cubes to the marinade and mix well until all the pieces are coated. Let it marinate for at least 2 hours or overnight for best results.\n3. Preheat the oven to 200°C (400°F).\n4. Thread the marinated chicken pieces onto skewers and place them on a baking tray lined with foil.\n5. Drizzle oil over the chicken and bake in the preheated oven for 20-25 minutes, or until the chicken is cooked through and slightly charred.\n6. Serve hot with naan bread, salad, and mint chutney.\n\nCalories: Approximately 350 kcal','Ingredients:\n- 500g boneless chicken, cut into cubes\n- 1 cup yogurt\n- 2 tbsp ginger-garlic paste\n- 1 tbsp red chili powder\n- 1 tsp turmeric powder\n- 1 tsp garam masala\n- 1 tbsp lemon juice\n- Salt to taste\n- 2 tbsp oil\n\nInstructions:\n1. In a bowl, mix yogurt, ginger-garlic paste, red chili powder, turmeric powder, garam masala, lemon juice, and salt.\n2. Add the chicken cubes to the marinade and mix well until all the pieces are coated. Let it marinate for at least 2 hours or overnight for best results.\n3. Preheat the oven to 200°C (400°F).\n4. Thread the marinated chicken pieces onto skewers and place them on a baking tray lined with foil.\n5. Drizzle oil over the chicken and bake in the preheated oven for 20-25 minutes, or until the chicken is cooked through and slightly charred.\n6. Serve hot with naan bread, salad, and mint chutney.\n\nCalories: Approximately 350 kcal','Not specified',NULL),(6,'pizza','- 1 pre-made pizza crust\n- 1 cup of cooked chicken tikka, shredded\n- 1 cup of mozzarella cheese\n- 1/2 cup of sliced onions\n- 1/2 cup of chopped bell peppers\n- 1/4 cup of sliced tomatoes\n- 2 tbsp of green chutney (coriander-mint sauce)\n- 1 tsp of chaat masala (spice mix)\n- 1 tsp of red chili powder','1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (200°C).\n2. Spread green chutney on the pre-made pizza crust.\n3. Evenly distribute the shredded chicken tikka on top of the chutney.\n4. Sprinkle mozzarella cheese over the chicken.\n5. Add the sliced onions, bell peppers, and tomatoes on top.\n6. Sprinkle chaat masala and red chili powder for extra flavor.\n7. Bake in the preheated oven for 15-20 minutes, or until the cheese is melted and bubbly.\n8. Slice and serve hot.\n\nCalories: Approximately 450 kcal (per serving)','Ingredients:\n- 1 pre-made pizza crust\n- 1 cup of cooked chicken tikka, shredded\n- 1 cup of mozzarella cheese\n- 1/2 cup of sliced onions\n- 1/2 cup of chopped bell peppers\n- 1/4 cup of sliced tomatoes\n- 2 tbsp of green chutney (coriander-mint sauce)\n- 1 tsp of chaat masala (spice mix)\n- 1 tsp of red chili powder\n\nInstructions:\n1. Preheat your oven to 400°F (200°C).\n2. Spread green chutney on the pre-made pizza crust.\n3. Evenly distribute the shredded chicken tikka on top of the chutney.\n4. Sprinkle mozzarella cheese over the chicken.\n5. Add the sliced onions, bell peppers, and tomatoes on top.\n6. Sprinkle chaat masala and red chili powder for extra flavor.\n7. Bake in the preheated oven for 15-20 minutes, or until the cheese is melted and bubbly.\n8. Slice and serve hot.\n\nCalories: Approximately 450 kcal (per serving)','Not specified',NULL);
